---
// Site-wide scripts that used to sit at the bottom of the original file:
// mobile nav/hamburger + scroll-spy + contact form handling, animated
// stat counters, the testimonials carousel (+ footer year + privacy
// modal), scroll-reveal animations, and cursor-parallax leaves. Loaded
// last, in the same relative order as the original markup, so every
// element they query already exists in the DOM above them.
//
// PERFORMANCE FIX: this used to also load the full AOS library from
// unpkg (unminified aos.js) and call AOS.init(). AOS's own stylesheet
// (aos.css) was never included anywhere in the project, so the classes
// AOS toggles on scroll had no CSS to act on — the 8 elements marked
// data-aos were receiving zero visible animation, while the page still
// paid for fetching/parsing the library and for AOS's scroll/resize/
// mutation observers running continuously. Removing it is a pure
// no-visual-change cleanup: those elements looked exactly the same
// before and after, since AOS was never actually animating them.
---
<script src="/scripts/aos-nav-contact.js" is:inline></script>
<script src="/scripts/counters.js" is:inline></script>
<script src="/scripts/carousel-footer-privacy.js" is:inline></script>
<script src="/scripts/reveal.js" is:inline></script>
<script src="/scripts/parallax.js" is:inline></script>
